# Line endings.
#
# Every file in this repo is written with LF, and the guard scripts in
# apps/mobile/scripts read source as text and match against it — several of them
# on multi-line literals. Without this file, Git on Windows checks the tree out
# with CRLF (`core.autocrlf=true` is that platform's installer default), the
# literals stop matching, and `pnpm check:all` fails on a machine where nothing
# is wrong.
#
# That failure is the worst shape a failure can have: invisible on the machine
# it was written on, fatal on the machine it runs on, and pointing at code that
# is perfectly correct. apps/mobile/scripts/check-scripts-portable.mjs exists
# for this whole class of bug — the path-separator version of it cost a build
# once already.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: decide what is text by content, and check every text
# file out with LF on every platform. Working trees are then byte-identical
# whatever anyone's Git is configured to do.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, so Git never inspects or rewrites them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
